+
+## The gateway, the adapters and the gate
+
+The engine is one model today (gpt-oss). The next increment puts a facade in front of it so a second model enters without touching the numeric path of the first. Three pieces, each with one job:
+
+| Piece | File | Job |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Extractor | `tools/inspect_model.py` | describes the structure: `layer_map.json` + `arch.json` (schema `arch-spec/1`) |
+| Adapter | `include/gptoss/adapter_gpt_oss.hpp` | implements one model: load, prefill, decode. Thin: every call goes to the `Model` already verified by the selfcheck |
+| Gateway | `include/gptoss/gateway.hpp` | routes: reads `arch.json`, validates the contract, finds the adapter in the registry, admits it only if the gate approved it |
+| Gate | `include/gptoss/gate.hpp` | certifies: an adapter is admitted only on `MATCH` against an independent reference, for the exact configuration |
+
+The architecture comes from `arch.json`, never from the directory name or a flag. There is no fallback: an architecture without an approved adapter stops before the inference, with a diagnostic that separates two different causes — a component the engine **does not run** (`arch/supported.json`) from a component whose **semantics are unknown** (a tensor no rule recognizes, a parameter the model's own files do not declare, a routing algorithm not stated). The first needs an adapter; the second needs the reference code read.
+
+`open(arch, dir)` — the path the original entry point used — is kept as it is, so `run_regression_test.sh` still tests the same thing. `open_from_spec(dir, opts, ref, diag)` is the new path: it derives the architecture from the spec and asks the gate.
+
+### What arch-spec/1 must carry, and what was missing
+
+Checked against the real gpt-oss-120b (36 layers, 687 tensors, 15 shards) and its `config.json`. The fields the first version had were not enough to write an adapter:
+
+- **No structural parameters.** An adapter needs hidden 2880, head_dim 64, 64 heads / 8 kv, window 128, YaRN factor 32 / beta 32-1 / orig 4096, theta 150000, `swiglu_limit` 7.0, `rms_norm_eps` 1e-5, vocab 201088, eos 200002. Added as `params`, each value with `{value, from, how}`: `declared` = the file says it, `deduced` = arithmetic from declared values (`head_dim = hidden / kv_heads`, only when the division is exact), otherwise the name goes to `unknown_params`. Nothing is guessed: on the real model `swiglu_alpha` and `bos` are **not** in `config.json`, and they stay in `unknown_params`.
+- **No `layer_types`.** The 36 layers of gpt-oss have **one** `layer_kind` — identical tensor names in every layer — while 18 are sliding and 18 are dense, alternating. `layer_kinds` groups by tensors and cannot express that. Added as `layer_types: {value, from}`, read from `config.json:layer_types` or the GGUF `*.attention.type`; when neither declares it, the spec says so.
+- **No tensor→component binding.** Added `component_evidence`: for each component rule, the tensor names that matched. A rule that matches the wrong tensor is then visible, not hidden behind a boolean. And `unbound_tensors`: stems that match no component rule and no standard role — for gpt-oss that list is empty, for an unrecognized model it is where the adapter work starts.
+- **No routing.** `config.json` does not state the routing algorithm (softmax, renormalize, bias order). The spec carries `routing.algorithm = "unknown"` and says to read it from the reference code. It is not invented.
+
+### The gate
+
+`arch/certifications.txt`, append-only, one line per verification: `arch | config | code-version | hash(arch.json) | hash(reference) | status`. A record authorizes a run only if all five match: the configuration fingerprint covers the flags that change the numeric path (`--cuda`, ctx, `--prefill-chunk`, `--gpu-attn`, `--prefill-dev-pct`, `-k`/`-v`, `--no-device-graphs`, `--no-async-dense`, `--glu-halves`, `--rope-pairs`, `--no-concentration`, `--vram-pct`, `--vram-reserve-mib`, `--pin-ram-gib`, `--expert-promote`), the spec is the same bytes, the reference is the same file, and `GATE_CODE_VERSION` has not moved. `NO_MATCH` and `INCONCLUSIVE` block the admission; writing the reference for the first time is `INCONCLUSIVE`, because no comparison happened. The gate certifies correctness within the tests run, not for every input.
+
+`--gate-info` answers, without loading the model, what the gateway would do with those flags.
+
+### What was run, and what was not
+
+Run on the emulated device with `tests/tiny` (4 layers, 8 experts, 96 vocab), same binary `build-out/gptoss_run_cpu_gate`:
+
+- `test_gptoss_core` on `tests/tiny`: `all ok` — the numeric path did not move.
+- `--gateway-info` (through the adapter) prints `GATEWAY_TOKENS 13,0,0,...` and the direct selfcheck prints `tokens 13,0,0,...`: identical sequences.
+- gate: first selfcheck writes the reference → record `INCONCLUSIVE`, gateway refuses; second selfcheck → `MATCH with the reference`, record `MATCH`, `--gate-info` with the same flags and the same `--selfcheck-file` → `status=MATCH ... gateway.open_from_spec -> adapter`; with one flag changed (`--ctx 48`) → `status=UNKNOWN ... refused`.
+- a directory without `arch.json` → `spec not valid: arch.json absent`; a spec with `"schema":"arch-spec/0"` → `schema 'arch-spec/0' not arch-spec/1`; `tests/gguf/test.gguf` (arch `test`) → `registered=0`, `not supported: architettura 'test' non registrata nel motore`, plus the list of unknown parameters. No fallback in any of the four.
+
+Not run: the CUDA selfcheck of gpt-oss-120b on the new binary. The GPU was occupied by another process (23790 MiB of 24564 MiB held by pid 2665405), so the run stopped at `cudaSetDevice: out of memory` after the load had printed the model card and the KV plan. The `MATCH` of the previous build belongs to the previous binary; it is not evidence about this one. To verify: `cd /home/albus/workspaces/RiStarta/Strata/gptoss_ext && NVCC=/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc bash build.sh --cuda && ./build-out/gptoss_run_cuda --model /media/albus/windows/Users/mio/models/llm_models/models/lmstudio-community/gpt-oss-120b --cuda --ctx 128000 --prefill-chunk 0 --vram-pct 97 --vram-reserve-mib 768 --expert-profile /var/tmp/gptoss-expert.bin --pin-ram-gib 58 -k e4m3 -v e4m3 --expert-promote 3 --selfcheck --selfcheck-file /var/tmp/selfcheck_ref.txt` — then `--gate-info` with the same flags must print `status=MATCH`.
+
+The multi-architecture support is not claimed: one adapter exists. A second model enters only with its own adapter and its own `MATCH`.
diff --git a/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/adapter.hpp b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/adapter.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..adde6fee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/adapter.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+// Interfaccia comune di ogni modello. Un adapter per modello implementa questa classe.
+#pragma once
+#include <functional>
+#include <memory>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace gptoss {
+
+struct ModelAdapter {
+    virtual ~ModelAdapter() = default;
+    virtual const char* arch() const = 0;   // architettura, uguale a "arch" in arch.json (arch-spec/1)
+    virtual int vocab() const = 0;
+    virtual void reset() = 0;
+    // Il prefill riempie la cache per le posizioni [pos0, pos0+n); i logit dell'ultimo token vanno in *logits.
+    virtual void prefill(const int* ids, int n, int pos0, std::vector<float>* logits) = 0;
+    // Decodifica di un token alla posizione pos.
+    virtual void forward(int token, int pos, std::vector<float>* logits) = 0;
+};
+
+// Costruisce un adapter dalla cartella del modello. Le opzioni (RunOpts, ecc.) sono catturate dalla factory.
+using AdapterFactory = std::function<std::unique_ptr<ModelAdapter>(const std::string& model_dir)>;
+
+}  // namespace gptoss
diff --git a/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/adapter_gpt_oss.hpp b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/adapter_gpt_oss.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..bdb239c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/adapter_gpt_oss.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+// Adapter di gpt-oss: avvolge gptoss::Model. Nessun calcolo nuovo: ogni chiamata va dritta al Model gia' verificato col selfcheck.
+#pragma once
+#include <memory>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <string>
+
+#include "adapter.hpp"
+#include "gateway.hpp"
+#include "model.hpp"
+
+namespace gptoss {
+
+class GptOssAdapter final : public ModelAdapter {
+public:
+    explicit GptOssAdapter(const RunOpts& o) : opts_(o) {}
+
+    bool open(const std::string& dir, std::string& err) { return m_.load(dir, opts_, err); }
+    Model& model() { return m_; }
+
+    const char* arch() const override { return m_.config().arch.c_str(); }
+    int vocab() const override { return m_.config().vocab; }
+    void reset() override { m_.reset(); }
+    void prefill(const int* ids, int n, int pos0, std::vector<float>* logits) override { m_.prefill(ids, n, pos0, logits); }
+    void forward(int token, int pos, std::vector<float>* logits) override { m_.forward(token, pos, logits); }
+
+private:
+    RunOpts opts_;
+    Model m_;
+};
+
+// Factory da registrare nel gateway: apre il modello con le opzioni del run.
+inline AdapterFactory gpt_oss_factory(const RunOpts& o) {
+    return [o](const std::string& dir) -> std::unique_ptr<ModelAdapter> {
+        auto a = std::make_unique<GptOssAdapter>(o);
+        std::string err;
+        if (!a->open(dir, err)) throw std::runtime_error("gpt_oss: " + err);
+        return a;
+    };
+}
+
+// Registra gpt_oss nel gateway (chiamare una volta all'avvio, con le RunOpts del run).
+inline void register_gpt_oss(const RunOpts& o) {
+    Gateway::instance().add("gpt_oss", gpt_oss_factory(o));
+}
+
+}  // namespace gptoss
diff --git a/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/arch_check.hpp b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/arch_check.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e246ef1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/arch_check.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+// arch_check.hpp - controlla arch.json (arch-spec/1) contro arch/supported.json: quali componenti mancano al motore. Header-only.
+#pragma once
+#include <fstream>
+#include <set>
+#include <sstream>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "json.hpp"
+
+namespace gptoss {
+
+struct SpecCheck {
+    bool found = false;                    // false = nessun arch.json: il controllo non si e' potuto fare
+    std::string arch;
+    std::vector<std::string> missing;      // componenti o caratteristiche che il motore non esegue
+    bool ok() const { return missing.empty(); }
+};
+
+// Componenti eseguiti per architettura, da arch/supported.json. Senza file (o illeggibile) usa la tabella di riserva.
+inline std::set<std::string> supported_components(const std::string& arch, const std::string& path = "arch/supported.json") {
+    std::ifstream in(path);
+    if (in) {
+        std::stringstream ss;
+        ss << in.rdbuf();
+        Json j;
+        std::string err;
+        if (parse_json(ss.str(), j, err)) {
+            std::set<std::string> out;
+            const Json* archs = j.get("architectures");
+            const Json* e = archs ? archs->get(arch) : nullptr;
+            const Json* c = e ? e->get("components") : nullptr;
+            if (c)
+                for (const auto& x : c->a)
+                    if (x.t == Json::Str) out.insert(x.s);
+            return out;
+        }
+    }
+    if (arch == "gpt_oss") return {"attention_sinks", "router_bias", "mxfp4_experts", "attention_bias"};
+    return {};
+}
+
+inline SpecCheck check_arch_spec(const std::string& model_dir, const std::string& arch_expected) {
+    SpecCheck r;
+    std::ifstream in(model_dir + "/arch.json");
+    if (!in) return r;
+    r.found = true;
+    std::stringstream ss;
+    ss << in.rdbuf();
+    Json j;
+    std::string err;
+    if (!parse_json(ss.str(), j, err)) {
+        r.missing.push_back("arch.json non leggibile: " + err);
+        return r;
+    }
+    r.arch = j.str("arch", "unknown");
+    if (r.arch != arch_expected)
+        r.missing.push_back("architettura '" + r.arch + "' (questo motore esegue '" + arch_expected + "')");
+    const std::set<std::string> sup = supported_components(r.arch);
+    if (const Json* c = j.get("components")) {
+        for (const auto& kv : c->o)
+            if (kv.second.t == Json::Bool && kv.second.b && !sup.count(kv.first))
+                r.missing.push_back("componente " + kv.first);
+    }
+    if (const Json* lk = j.get("layer_kinds")) {
+        if (lk->a.size() > 1 && !sup.count("multiple_layer_kinds"))
+            r.missing.push_back("layer di " + std::to_string(lk->a.size()) + " tipi diversi");
+    }
+    return r;
+}
+
+}  // namespace gptoss
diff --git a/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/attn_dsv4.hpp b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/attn_dsv4.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..82df2745
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/attn_dsv4.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,254 @@
+// attn_dsv4.hpp - attenzione DeepSeek-V4 in CPU, percorso RAW (layer con compress_ratio == 0).
+// Port di build_attention_impl (righe 878-1220) e build_raw_attention (righe 824-858) di deepseek4.cpp.
+// Copre: proiezione q (q-LoRA), proiezione kv, RoPE parziale, attenzione con sink e finestra SWA, output a gruppi.
+// NON coperti (blocco successivo): compressori CSA/HCA, indexer lightning e top-k, stato delle cache.
+//
+// ASSUNZIONI da confermare (il sorgente non le dichiara direttamente nel file ricevuto):
+//  A1 rope_type: NEOX, cioè coppie (i, i + n_rot/2) dentro la porzione di rope. Parametro: AttnParams::neox
+//     (oggi il ramo non-NEOX non è implementato: lo stop esplicito evita di indovinarlo in silenzio).
+//  A2 attn_sinks: un logit per testa nel softmax, il sink non contribuisce al valore (build_attn_mha non è nel file).
+//  A3 finestra SWA: chiavi j con t - n_swa < j <= t.
+//  A4 Hadamard k_rot del percorso raw: omesso. Se la matrice è ortonormale, q·k e l'output si annullano.
+//  A5 wo_a con layout GGML [o_group_dim, o_lora_rank, n_groups]: riga r + g*o_lora_rank, colonne contigue.
+//  A6 attn_sinks tipo F32.
+//  A7 rope: mscale = attn_factor, come calcolato da dsv4_rope_attn_factor nel sorgente.
+//
+// Layout: head-major. Testa h del token t inizia a (t*n_head + h)*head_dim. Il RoPE agisce sugli ultimi n_rot
+// valori di ogni testa (offset nope = head_dim - n_rot), come ggml_rope_set_offset.
+#pragma once
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "gptoss/cpu_matvec.hpp"
+#include "gptoss/dequant_registry.hpp"
+#include "gptoss/hc_ops.hpp"  // gptoss::rms_norm_plain
+
+namespace gptoss::dsv4 {
+
+struct AttnParams {
+    int64_t n_embd = 4096;
+    int64_t n_head = 64;
+    int64_t head_dim = 512;        // n_embd_head_k (= n_embd_head_v)
+    int64_t n_rot = 64;            // hparams.n_rot()          DA LEGGERE dal GGUF
+    int64_t n_lora_q = 1024;       // LLM_KV_ATTENTION_Q_LORA_RANK
+    int64_t n_groups = 8;          // dsv4_o_group_count
+    int64_t o_lora_rank = 1024;    // dsv4_o_lora_rank
+    int64_t n_swa = 128;           // n_swa                    DA LEGGERE dal GGUF
+    float rms_eps = 1e-6f;         // f_norm_rms_eps           DA LEGGERE dal GGUF
+    // RoPE globale (layer non compressi usano freq_base, compressi usano compress_rope_base)
+    float freq_base = 10000.0f;    // DA LEGGERE
+    float compress_rope_base = 160000.0f;  // dsv4_compress_rope_base  DA LEGGERE
+    float freq_scale = 1.0f;       // DA LEGGERE (scala YaRN)
+    float ext_factor = 0.0f;       // DA LEGGERE (YaRN)
+    float beta_fast = 32.0f;       // DA LEGGERE (YaRN)
+    float beta_slow = 1.0f;        // DA LEGGERE (YaRN)
+    float n_ctx_orig = 0.0f;       // n_ctx_orig               DA LEGGERE
+    bool neox = true;              // A1
+};
+
+// Pesi quantizzati di un matrice in GGML: in = ne[0], out = ne[1], righe contigue.
+struct QuantMat {
+    const uint8_t* data = nullptr;
+    int type = 0;
+    int64_t in = 0;
+    int64_t out = 0;
+};
+
+struct AttnWeights {
+    QuantMat wq_a;                 // [n_embd -> n_lora_q]
+    QuantMat wq_b;                 // [n_lora_q -> n_head*head_dim]
+    QuantMat wkv;                  // [n_embd -> head_dim]
+    QuantMat wo_a;                 // [o_group_dim -> o_lora_rank*n_groups] (A5)
+    QuantMat wo_b;                 // [o_lora_rank*n_groups -> n_embd]
+    const float* q_a_norm = nullptr;   // attn_q_a_norm, peso di dimensione n_lora_q
+    const float* kv_norm = nullptr;    // attn_kv_norm,  peso di dimensione head_dim
+    const float* sinks = nullptr;      // attn_sinks,    dimensione n_head (A6)
+};
+
+// Configurazione RoPE per layer (come nelle righe 902-909 del sorgente).
+struct RopeCfg {
+    float base = 10000.0f;
+    float scale = 1.0f;
+    float ext = 0.0f;
+    float attn = 1.0f;
+    float beta_fast = 0.0f;
+    float beta_slow = 0.0f;
+    float n_ctx_orig = 0.0f;
+};
+
+inline float dsv4_rope_attn_factor(float freq_scale, float ext_factor) {
+    if (ext_factor == 0.0f) return 1.0f;
+    return 1.0f / (1.0f + 0.1f * std::log(1.0f / freq_scale));
+}
+
+inline RopeCfg rope_cfg_for_layer(const AttnParams& p, bool compressed) {
+    RopeCfg c;
+    if (compressed) {
+        c.base = p.compress_rope_base;
+        c.scale = p.freq_scale;
+        c.ext = p.ext_factor;
+        c.attn = dsv4_rope_attn_factor(c.scale, c.ext);
+        c.beta_fast = p.beta_fast;
+        c.beta_slow = p.beta_slow;
+        c.n_ctx_orig = p.n_ctx_orig;
+    } else {
+        c.base = p.freq_base;
+        c.scale = 1.0f;
+        c.ext = 0.0f;
+        c.attn = 1.0f;
+        c.beta_fast = 0.0f;
+        c.beta_slow = 0.0f;
+        c.n_ctx_orig = 0.0f;
+    }
+    return c;
+}
+
+// RMS norm con peso per elemento. y può coincidere con x.
+inline void rms_norm_weighted(const float* x, int64_t n, const float* w, float eps, float* y) {
+    double s = 0.0;
+    for (int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) s += (double) x[i] * x[i];
+    const float inv = 1.0f / std::sqrt((float) (s / (double) n) + eps);
+    for (int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) y[i] = x[i] * inv * w[i];
+}
+
+// Rampa YaRN (ggml_rope_yarn_ramp). i = indice della coppia (i0/2 in ggml).
+inline float yarn_ramp(float low, float high, int64_t i) {
+    const float y = ((float) i - low) / std::fmax(0.001f, high - low);
+    return 1.0f - std::fmin(1.0f, std::fmax(0.0f, y));
+}
+
+inline float yarn_corr_dim(float n_dims, float n_ctx_orig, float n_rot, float base) {
+    return n_dims * std::log(n_ctx_orig / (n_rot * 2.0f * 3.14159265358979323846f)) / (2.0f * std::log(base));
+}
+
+// RoPE parziale su v (lunghezza head_dim): ruota gli ultimi n_rot valori. inverse = ggml_rope_ext_back.
+inline void rope_apply(float* v, const AttnParams& p, const RopeCfg& c, int64_t pos, bool inverse) {
+    const int64_t n_rot = p.n_rot;
+    const int64_t off = p.head_dim - n_rot;
+    const int64_t half = n_rot / 2;
+
+    if (!p.neox) return;  // A1: il ramo non-NEOX non è implementato
+
+    float corr_lo = 0.0f, corr_hi = 0.0f;
+    const bool yarn = c.ext != 0.0f;
+    if (yarn) {
+        corr_lo = std::fmax(0.0f, std::floor(yarn_corr_dim((float) n_rot, c.n_ctx_orig, c.beta_fast, c.base)));
+        corr_hi = std::fmin((float) (n_rot - 1), std::ceil(yarn_corr_dim((float) n_rot, c.n_ctx_orig, c.beta_slow, c.base)));
+    }
+
+    for (int64_t i = 0; i < half; ++i) {
+        const float theta_extrap = (float) pos * std::pow(c.base, -2.0f * (float) i / (float) n_rot);
+        float theta = c.scale * theta_extrap;
+        if (yarn) {
+            const float mix = yarn_ramp(corr_lo, corr_hi, i) * c.ext;
+            theta = theta * (1.0f - mix) + theta_extrap * mix;
+        }
+        const float cs = std::cos(theta) * c.attn;
+        float sn = std::sin(theta) * c.attn;
+        if (inverse) sn = -sn;
+
+        float& a = v[off + i];
+        float& b = v[off + i + half];
+        const float na = a * cs - b * sn;
+        const float nb = a * sn + b * cs;
+        a = na;
+        b = nb;
+    }
+}
+
+// Attenzione raw con sink e finestra SWA. q: [T][n_head][head_dim], k: [T][head_dim] (k == v, MQA a una testa).
+// out: [T][n_head][head_dim]. Scala = 1/sqrt(head_dim) (come nel sorgente).
+inline void attn_core_raw(const AttnParams& p, const float* q, const float* k, int64_t T, const float* sinks, float* out) {
+    const int64_t H = p.n_head, D = p.head_dim;
+    const float scale = 1.0f / std::sqrt((float) D);
+    std::vector<float> s;
+    for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+        const int64_t j0 = std::max<int64_t>(0, t - p.n_swa + 1);
+        for (int64_t h = 0; h < H; ++h) {
+            const float* qh = q + (t * H + h) * D;
+            s.clear();
+            float mx = sinks[h];
+            for (int64_t j = j0; j <= t; ++j) {
+                const float* kj = k + j * D;
+                float dot = 0.0f;
+                for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) dot += qh[d] * kj[d];
+                dot *= scale;
+                s.push_back(dot);
+                if (dot > mx) mx = dot;
+            }
+            float denom = std::exp(sinks[h] - mx);
+            float* oh = out + (t * H + h) * D;
+            for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) oh[d] = 0.0f;
+            for (size_t idx = 0; idx < s.size(); ++idx) {
+                const int64_t j = j0 + (int64_t) idx;
+                const float w = std::exp(s[idx] - mx);
+                denom += w;
+                const float* vj = k + j * D;  // v == k
+                for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) oh[d] += w * vj[d];
+            }
+            const float inv = 1.0f / denom;
+            for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) oh[d] *= inv;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+// Proiezioni q e kv per un token. x: [n_embd]. q: [n_head*head_dim], kv: [head_dim].
+inline void attn_project_qkv(const AttnParams& p, const AttnWeights& w, const float* x, int64_t pos, bool compressed,
+                             float* q, float* kv, std::vector<float>& buf) {
+    const RopeCfg rc = rope_cfg_for_layer(p, compressed);
+    const int64_t H = p.n_head, D = p.head_dim;
+
+    std::vector<float> qr(static_cast<size_t>(p.n_lora_q));
+    matvec_quant(w.wq_a.type, w.wq_a.data, p.n_embd, p.n_lora_q, x, qr.data(), buf);
+    rms_norm_weighted(qr.data(), p.n_lora_q, w.q_a_norm, p.rms_eps, qr.data());
+
+    matvec_quant(w.wq_b.type, w.wq_b.data, p.n_lora_q, H * D, qr.data(), q, buf);
+    for (int64_t h = 0; h < H; ++h) {
+        float* qh = q + h * D;
+        gptoss::rms_norm_plain(qh, D, p.rms_eps, qh);  // norma per testa, senza peso
+        rope_apply(qh, p, rc, pos, false);
+    }
+
+    matvec_quant(w.wkv.type, w.wkv.data, p.n_embd, D, x, kv, buf);
+    rms_norm_weighted(kv, D, w.kv_norm, p.rms_eps, kv);
+    rope_apply(kv, p, rc, pos, false);
+}
+
+// Output di un token: derope inverso, wo_a per gruppi, wo_b. o: [n_head*head_dim] (modificato in copia interna).
+inline void attn_project_out(const AttnParams& p, const AttnWeights& w, const float* o, int64_t pos, bool compressed,
+                             float* out_embd, std::vector<float>& buf) {
+    const RopeCfg rc = rope_cfg_for_layer(p, compressed);
+    const int64_t H = p.n_head, D = p.head_dim, G = p.n_groups;
+    const int64_t nhg = H / G;
+    const int64_t og = nhg * D;  // o_group_dim
+
+    std::vector<float> ob(o, o + H * D);
+    for (int64_t h = 0; h < H; ++h) rope_apply(ob.data() + h * D, p, rc, pos, true);
+
+    std::vector<float> oa(static_cast<size_t>(p.o_lora_rank * G));
+    const size_t rb = dequant_row_bytes(w.wo_a.type, og);
+    for (int64_t g = 0; g < G; ++g) {
+        matvec_quant(w.wo_a.type, w.wo_a.data + static_cast<size_t>(g * p.o_lora_rank) * rb, og, p.o_lora_rank,
+                     ob.data() + g * og, oa.data() + g * p.o_lora_rank, buf);
+    }
+    matvec_quant(w.wo_b.type, w.wo_b.data, p.o_lora_rank * G, p.n_embd, oa.data(), out_embd, buf);
+}
+
+// Layer raw completo su T token (prefill senza cache). X: [T][n_embd] -> Y: [T][n_embd].
+inline void attn_forward_raw(const AttnParams& p, const AttnWeights& w, const float* X, int64_t T, float* Y) {
+    const int64_t H = p.n_head, D = p.head_dim;
+    std::vector<float> q(static_cast<size_t>(T * H * D)), kv(static_cast<size_t>(T * D));
+    std::vector<float> o(static_cast<size_t>(T * H * D));
+    std::vector<float> buf;
+    for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+        attn_project_qkv(p, w, X + t * p.n_embd, t, false, q.data() + t * H * D, kv.data() + t * D, buf);
+    }
+    attn_core_raw(p, q.data(), kv.data(), T, w.sinks, o.data());
+    for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+        attn_project_out(p, w, o.data() + t * H * D, t, false, Y + t * p.n_embd, buf);
+    }
+}
+
+}  // namespace gptoss::dsv4
diff --git a/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/attn_dsv4_comp.hpp b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/attn_dsv4_comp.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..58861178
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gptoss_ext/include/gptoss/attn_dsv4_comp.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,233 @@
+// attn_dsv4_comp.hpp - attenzione DeepSeek-V4 in CPU per i layer compressi (compress_ratio 4 = CSA con indexer,
+// 128 = HCA), in modalità prefill su sequenza intera, senza cache.
+// Port di build_overlap_compressed_kv_from_state / build_hca_compressed_kv_from_state (righe 470-588),
+// build_lid_top_k (590-676), build_top_k_mask (678-705), build_csa_lid_attention (707-767), build_hca_attention (769-822).
+// Richiede attn_dsv4.hpp per il percorso raw, le proiezioni e l'output.
+//
+// Il percorso di decodifica incrementale (cache raw, stati dei compressori) NON è coperto: qui la compressione
+// viene ricalcolata sull'intera sequenza, che è equivalente per il prefill.
+//
+// ASSUNZIONI aggiuntive da confermare (non deducibili dal file ricevuto, che non contiene la costruzione delle maschere
+// né degli input):
+//  A8  comp_pos del blocco b = b * ratio (primo token del blocco). Con questo valore il RoPE delle chiavi compresse è
+//      definito solo se l'input builder usa la stessa convenzione.
+//  A9  visibilità causale dei blocchi compressi: il blocco b è visibile al token t se (b+1)*ratio <= t+1 (blocco completo).
+//      Vale sia per l'indexer sia per HCA.
+//  A10 ape: la riga è indicizzata da (t mod ratio), cioè la posizione dentro il blocco.
+//  A11 compressione overlap (CSA): per il blocco b, metà 0 dei token del blocco b-1 e metà 1 dei token del blocco b.
+//      Per b = 0 la parte "precedente" è esclusa (score -inf nel sorgente).
+//  A12 indexer: le rotazioni Hadamard (k_rot) di indexer_q e delle chiavi si annullano nel prodotto scalare se sono
+//      ortonormali, quindi sono omesse. Il punteggio è sum_h w_h * relu(q_h · k) con w già scalato da 1/sqrt(IH*NH).
+//  A13 indexer_top_k: DA LEGGERE dal GGUF (LLM_KV_ATTENTION_INDEXER_TOP_K).
+#pragma once
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <limits>
+#include <utility>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "gptoss/attn_dsv4.hpp"
+
+namespace gptoss::dsv4 {
+
+// Pesi di un compressore (attn_comp_* oppure indexer_comp_*).
+struct CompWeights {
+    QuantMat wkv;               // [n_embd -> width]
+    QuantMat wgate;             // [n_embd -> width]
+    const float* ape = nullptr; // [ratio][width]  (A10)
+    const float* norm = nullptr;// [head]
+    int64_t head = 0;           // dimensione per testa del compressore
+    int64_t width = 0;          // head (senza overlap) oppure 2*head (overlap CSA)
+};
+
+struct IdxWeights {
+    QuantMat wq_b;              // indexer_attn_q_b [n_lora_q -> n_idx_head*idx_head]
+    QuantMat proj;              // indexer_proj     [n_embd -> n_idx_head]
+    CompWeights comp;           // indexer_comp_*   (head = idx_head, overlap)
+    int64_t n_idx_head = 64;    // indexer_n_head
+    int64_t idx_head = 128;     // indexer_head_size
+};
+
+struct CompLayer {
+    int64_t ratio = 0;          // 0 raw, 4 CSA (con indexer), 128 HCA
+    CompWeights comp;           // attn_comp_*  (usato se ratio != 0)
+    IdxWeights idx;             // solo se ratio == 4
+    int64_t indexer_top_k = 512;  // A13
+};
+
+inline AttnParams with_head_dim(const AttnParams& p, int64_t hd) {
+    AttnParams q = p;
+    q.head_dim = hd;
+    return q;
+}
+
+// qr = rms_norm(wq_a · x): il latente q normalizzato, che alimenta sia wq_b sia indexer_attn_q_b.
+inline void latent_q(const AttnParams& p, const AttnWeights& w, const float* x, float* qr_out, std::vector<float>& buf) {
+    matvec_quant(w.wq_a.type, w.wq_a.data, p.n_embd, p.n_lora_q, x, qr_out, buf);
+    rms_norm_weighted(qr_out, p.n_lora_q, w.q_a_norm, p.rms_eps, qr_out);
+}
+
+// Compressione a blocchi di tutta la sequenza. X: [T][n_embd] -> out: [T/ratio][head] (RoPE applicato, A8).
+inline void compress_sequence(const AttnParams& p, const CompWeights& c, int64_t ratio, int64_t T, const float* X,
+                              float* out, std::vector<float>& buf) {
+    const bool overlap = c.width == 2 * c.head;
+    const int64_t H = c.head, W = c.width, E = p.n_embd;
+    const int64_t nb = T / ratio;
+    const RopeCfg rc = rope_cfg_for_layer(p, true);
+    const AttnParams pc = with_head_dim(p, H);
+
+    std::vector<float> kvt(static_cast<size_t>(T * W)), sct(static_cast<size_t>(T * W));
+    for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+        matvec_quant(c.wkv.type, c.wkv.data, E, W, X + t * E, kvt.data() + t * W, buf);
+        matvec_quant(c.wgate.type, c.wgate.data, E, W, X + t * E, sct.data() + t * W, buf);
+        const float* a = c.ape + (t % ratio) * W;  // A10
+        for (int64_t j = 0; j < W; ++j) sct[t * W + j] += a[j];
+    }
+
+    std::vector<float> sc, vl;
+    for (int64_t b = 0; b < nb; ++b) {
+        float* cb = out + b * H;
+        for (int64_t d = 0; d < H; ++d) {
+            sc.clear();
+            vl.clear();
+            if (!overlap) {
+                for (int64_t i = 0; i < ratio; ++i) {
+                    const int64_t t = b * ratio + i;
+                    sc.push_back(sct[t * W + d]);
+                    vl.push_back(kvt[t * W + d]);
+                }
+            } else {
+                if (b > 0) {  // A11: metà 0 del blocco precedente
+                    for (int64_t i = 0; i < ratio; ++i) {
+                        const int64_t t = (b - 1) * ratio + i;
+                        sc.push_back(sct[t * W + d]);
+                        vl.push_back(kvt[t * W + d]);
+                    }
+                }
+                for (int64_t i = 0; i < ratio; ++i) {  // metà 1 del blocco corrente
+                    const int64_t t = b * ratio + i;
+                    sc.push_back(sct[t * W + H + d]);
+                    vl.push_back(kvt[t * W + H + d]);
+                }
+            }
+            float mx = -std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
+            for (float s : sc) mx = std::max(mx, s);
+            float den = 0.0f, num = 0.0f;
+            for (size_t k = 0; k < sc.size(); ++k) {
+                const float wgt = std::exp(sc[k] - mx);
+                den += wgt;
+                num += wgt * vl[k];
+            }
+            cb[d] = num / den;
+        }
+        rms_norm_weighted(cb, H, c.norm, p.rms_eps, cb);
+        rope_apply(cb, pc, rc, b * ratio, false);  // A8
+    }
+}
+
+// Visibilità causale di un blocco compresso (A9).
+inline bool comp_block_visible(int64_t b, int64_t t, int64_t ratio) { return (b + 1) * ratio <= t + 1; }
+
+// Layer compresso completo su T token (prefill). X: [T][n_embd] -> Y: [T][n_embd].
+inline void attn_forward_layer(const AttnParams& p, const AttnWeights& w, const CompLayer& L, const float* X, int64_t T,
+                               float* Y) {
+    const int64_t H = p.n_head, D = p.head_dim, E = p.n_embd, NQ = p.n_lora_q;
+    const bool compressed = L.ratio != 0;
+    std::vector<float> buf;
+    std::vector<float> qr(static_cast<size_t>(T * NQ)), q(static_cast<size_t>(T * H * D));
+    std::vector<float> kv(static_cast<size_t>(T * D)), o(static_cast<size_t>(T * H * D));
+
+    for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+        latent_q(p, w, X + t * E, qr.data() + t * NQ, buf);
+        attn_project_qkv(p, w, X + t * E, t, compressed, q.data() + t * H * D, kv.data() + t * D, buf);
+    }
+
+    if (!compressed) {
+        attn_core_raw(p, q.data(), kv.data(), T, w.sinks, o.data());
+    } else {
+        const int64_t nb = T / L.ratio;
+        std::vector<float> comp(static_cast<size_t>(nb * D));
+        compress_sequence(p, L.comp, L.ratio, T, X, comp.data(), buf);
+
+        std::vector<std::vector<int64_t>> sel(static_cast<size_t>(T));
+        if (L.ratio == 4) {  // CSA: indexer + top-k
+            const AttnParams ip = with_head_dim(p, L.idx.idx_head);
+            const int64_t NI = L.idx.n_idx_head, IH = L.idx.idx_head;
+            std::vector<float> idk(static_cast<size_t>(nb * IH));
+            compress_sequence(ip, L.idx.comp, 4, T, X, idk.data(), buf);
+            const RopeCfg rci = rope_cfg_for_layer(p, true);
+            const float wscale = 1.0f / std::sqrt((float) (IH * NI));
+            std::vector<float> qi(static_cast<size_t>(NI * IH)), wt(static_cast<size_t>(NI));
+            for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+                matvec_quant(L.idx.wq_b.type, L.idx.wq_b.data, NQ, NI * IH, qr.data() + t * NQ, qi.data(), buf);
+                for (int64_t h = 0; h < NI; ++h) rope_apply(qi.data() + h * IH, ip, rci, t, false);
+                matvec_quant(L.idx.proj.type, L.idx.proj.data, E, NI, X + t * E, wt.data(), buf);
+                for (int64_t h = 0; h < NI; ++h) wt[h] *= wscale;
+
+                std::vector<std::pair<float, int64_t>> cand;
+                for (int64_t b = 0; b < nb; ++b) {
+                    if (!comp_block_visible(b, t, 4)) continue;
+                    float s = 0.0f;
+                    for (int64_t h = 0; h < NI; ++h) {
+                        float dot = 0.0f;
+                        for (int64_t d = 0; d < IH; ++d) dot += qi[h * IH + d] * idk[b * IH + d];
+                        if (dot > 0.0f) s += wt[h] * dot;  // relu
+                    }
+                    cand.emplace_back(s, b);
+                }
+                const int64_t K = std::min<int64_t>((int64_t) cand.size(), L.indexer_top_k);
+                std::partial_sort(cand.begin(), cand.begin() + K, cand.end(),
+                                  [](const std::pair<float, int64_t>& a, const std::pair<float, int64_t>& b) {
+                                      return a.first > b.first;
+                                  });
+                for (int64_t k = 0; k < K; ++k) sel[t].push_back(cand[k].second);
+            }
+        } else {  // HCA (ratio 128): tutti i blocchi visibili
+            for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+                for (int64_t b = 0; b < nb; ++b) {
+                    if (comp_block_visible(b, t, L.ratio)) sel[t].push_back(b);
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
+        // Attenzione: chiavi = finestra raw SWA + blocchi compressi selezionati. v = k. Sink come nel percorso raw.
+        const float scale = 1.0f / std::sqrt((float) D);
+        std::vector<const float*> rows;
+        std::vector<float> sc;
+        for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+            rows.clear();
+            const int64_t j0 = std::max<int64_t>(0, t - p.n_swa + 1);
+            for (int64_t j = j0; j <= t; ++j) rows.push_back(kv.data() + j * D);
+            for (int64_t b : sel[t]) rows.push_back(comp.data() + b * D);
+            for (int64_t h = 0; h < H; ++h) {
+                const float* qh = q.data() + (t * H + h) * D;
+                sc.clear();
+                float mx = w.sinks[h];
+                for (const float* kr : rows) {
+                    float dot = 0.0f;
+                    for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) dot += qh[d] * kr[d];
+                    dot *= scale;
+                    sc.push_back(dot);
+                    mx = std::max(mx, dot);
+                }
+                float den = std::exp(w.sinks[h] - mx);
+                float* oh = o.data() + (t * H + h) * D;
+                for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) oh[d] = 0.0f;
+                for (size_t k = 0; k < rows.size(); ++k) {
+                    const float wgt = std::exp(sc[k] - mx);
+                    den += wgt;
+                    for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) oh[d] += wgt * rows[k][d];
+                }
+                const float inv = 1.0f / den;
+                for (int64_t d = 0; d < D; ++d) oh[d] *= inv;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    for (int64_t t = 0; t < T; ++t) {
+        attn_project_out(p, w, o.data() + t * H * D, t, compressed, Y + t * E, buf);
+    }
+}
+
+}  // namespace gptoss::dsv4
